package kgen

func init() {
	opsEntries = append(opsEntries,
		opsDoc{"pred:NamedCard", "PredNamedCard", "The candidate's card is the reading source's chosen card name (gorge Card.NamedCard, effects/filter.go namePredicate): a battlefield source's chosen byte (ExtChooseName or ExtNameCard), a stack source's this resolution's ExtNameCard answer, and a host-bound emblem static's frozen capture (gorge state.ContinuousEffect.ChosenName + ChosenNameFrozen, the name the source carried when the Effect registered), read once an ExtClearNamedCard chain wiped the source after (Cheering Fanatic's ReduceCost). A face-down candidate matches nothing, and a source with no chosen name matches nothing, as gorge's empty ChosenName does. FilterFlags2 is full, so the word takes the one Pred slot. Demonic Consultation's DigUntil Valid$ Card.NamedCard, Cheering Fanatic's ReduceCost ValidCard$ Card.NamedCard, Comply's CantBeCast ValidCard$ Card.nonLand+NamedCard, Silverquill Silencer's SpellCast trigger."},
		opsDoc{"ext:NameCard", "OpExt ExtNameCard (B.N)", "A mid-resolution card-name choice, the whole api node (CR 201.4; gorge effects/cardflow.go effNameCard, `SP$ NameCard` / `DB$ NameCard`): the resolving controller chooses the name of one real card of the matchup (a ChGenName decision, mode = its CardID, Table.NameCardsAny ascending, or Table.NameCards when B.N = 1, gorge ValidCards$ Card.nonLand, gorge's sorted name list over the matchup's name universe), and the answer is stored on the resolving source: a battlefield source keeps it in its chosen byte (the ExtChooseName slot, gorge's one Object.ChosenName), a source still on the stack keeps it in the resolution's own answer (gorge clears the name when an object leaves the battlefield, so a spell's name needs nothing past its chain; dirac/repl_namecard.go). The ask is skipped when the source already carries a name (gorge effNameCard's `o.ChosenName != \"\"` guard), and with no eligible name it asks nothing, as gorge returns on an empty list. ValidCards$ names only the empty string or Card.nonLand; a ValidDescription$-narrowed ask refuses unless the description is one of gorge's known non-narrowing ones (the descriptionSpecTab fallback). AtRandom$, ChooseFromList$, ChooseFromDefinedCards$ and ExcludeChosen$ refuse. Read by PredNamedCard; emptied by ExtClearNamedCard. Demonic Consultation (B.N = 0), Cabal Therapist, Cabal Therapy, Mise, Mindblaze (B.N = 1)."},
		opsDoc{"ext:ClearNamedCard", "OpExt ExtClearNamedCard", "Empties the resolving source's chosen card name (gorge `DB$ Cleanup | ClearNamedCard$ True`): the next ExtNameCard on the same source asks anew, as gorge's wiped Object.ChosenName does. Cheering Fanatic's trigger body names, registers its ReduceCost Effect (whose static keeps the name frozen), then clears. No decision."},
	)
}
